;; check:fcis allowlist — genuine FC/IS debt only.
;;
;; The gate (bb check:fcis) bans (throw ...) and mutable state (defonce, atom,
;; swap!, reset!, …) in core namespaces.
;;
;; Namespaces that LEGITIMATELY need an exception are exempted INLINE via
;; ^:wagoe/allow-throw / ^:wagoe/allow-mutable-state ns metadata, with the
;; rationale next to the code (wagoe.core.interceptor, the validation-testing
;; tooling, and wagoe.platform.core.search.ranking).
;;
;; This file is reserved for REAL debt to migrate. There is none right now — the
;; validation rule registry's mutable state moved to
;; wagoe.platform.shell.validation-registry in BOU-188. Add an entry here only
;; as a temporary allowance while a new violation is being migrated out.
;; :allow-require is per-namespace AND per-require, and every entry needs a
;; :why. Since BOU-301 the require check is an allowlist — a core namespace may
;; require pure libraries and its own core/schema/ports, and nothing else — so
;; this is where a justified exception to that goes.
{:allow-throw         []
 :allow-mutable-state []
 :allow-require
 [{:ns      wagoe.core.validation.behavior
   :require clojure.test
   :why     "A behaviour-spec DSL whose output is deftest forms, so clojure.test
             is its vocabulary rather than a dependency it reaches for. The
             functions that build scenarios are pure; only the macro that
             expands them emits tests. Moving it out would put a testing DSL in
             the shell, where nothing else about testing lives."}]}
